{"changed_files":["packages/core/router/utils/flatten-route-paths.util.ts","packages/core/test/router/utils/flat-routes.spec.ts"],"changed_functions":["flattenRoutePaths"],"child_sha":"8cbbcf4074917b858733029d601dc3c0be482c74","filters_passed":["developer_intent","not_revert","not_merge","source_file_limit","function_limit","no_public_feature_addition","parse_before_after","not_generated","null_detector"],"intent_evidence":{"linked_issues":[],"message":"fix(core): Make flattenRoutePath return a valid module\n\nflattenRoutePath method was returning an object instead of a module when path property was an empty string\n\ncloses #15332"},"language":"typescript","license":"MIT","pair_group":{"id":"refactor-c41d8672c97b56d6","kind":"refactor","repository":"nestjs/nest","samples":["8cbbcf4074917b858733029d601dc3c0be482c74:before","8cbbcf4074917b858733029d601dc3c0be482c74:after"]},"pair_group_id":"refactor-c41d8672c97b56d6","parent_sha":"84d0ff32bc1fc4306d0fb270cbaf5b4ddf2decb9","pin_sha":"2eb7be8dc3410ac5b89aa84fd334e6813b53059c","repo":"nestjs/nest"}
{"changed_files":["packages/core/nest-application-context.ts","packages/core/test/nest-application-context.spec.ts"],"changed_functions":["removeListenersNotIn","signals"],"child_sha":"ddbb455220b3099d67ee6d4a816528f9a6c0fab1","filters_passed":["developer_intent","not_revert","not_merge","source_file_limit","function_limit","no_public_feature_addition","parse_before_after","not_generated","null_detector"],"intent_evidence":{"linked_issues":[],"message":"fix(core): clean up repeated shutdown signal listeners (#17625)\n\n* fix(core): clean up repeated shutdown signal listeners\n\nTrack each registered cleanup handler and share shutdown state across\nregistrations so close removes every process listener and concurrent signals run\nhooks once.\n\nCloses #17623\n\n* test(core): cover repeated shutdown hook registration\n\nAdd a regression for the same signal registered by separate calls and\nassert listener counts before and after cleanup. Share baseline cleanup,\nuse the handler map consistently, and document registration behavior.\nReset the shutdown guard alongside listener cleanup.\n\n* fix(core): run the shutdown sequence once per cycle\n\nPromoting the received-signal guard to instance scope stopped concurrent\nsignals from tearing the context down twice, but `close()` never took part\nin it. A signal delivered while a programmatic `close()` was still awaiting\nits hooks re-entered the cleanup handler with the guard clear and ran\n`callDestroyHook`, `callBeforeShutdownHook`, `dispose` and\n`callShutdownHook` a second time, concurrently.\n\nReplace the boolean with the in-flight shutdown promise itself and share it\nbetween both entry points, so whichever arrives second awaits the first\ninstead of starting its own teardown. The sequence moves into\n`runShutdownSequence`, which `close()` and the signal handler now reach\nthrough `shutdown()` rather than each keeping their own copy of the six\nlifecycle calls.\n\nClearing the promise once the cycle settles also unwedges the failure path:\npreviously a throw skipped `unsubscribeFromProcessSignals`, leaving the flag\nlatched and the registry populated, so the reset in `enableShutdownHooks`\ncould never fire and the context ignored every later signal.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Kamil My\u015bliwiec <mail@kamilmysliwiec.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>"},"language":"typescript","license":"MIT","pair_group":{"id":"refactor-e0a816dadf8e37af","kind":"refactor","repository":"nestjs/nest","samples":["ddbb455220b3099d67ee6d4a816528f9a6c0fab1:before","ddbb455220b3099d67ee6d4a816528f9a6c0fab1:after"]},"pair_group_id":"refactor-e0a816dadf8e37af","parent_sha":"eb65d75ec42c153f1da5e4ef5499ee95e91dbb9e","pin_sha":"2eb7be8dc3410ac5b89aa84fd334e6813b53059c","repo":"nestjs/nest"}
{"changed_files":["integration/send-files/e2e/express.spec.ts","packages/platform-express/adapters/express-adapter.ts","packages/platform-express/test/adapters/express-adapter.spec.ts"],"changed_functions":["it","read","reply","write"],"child_sha":"8b8e8396f71d8903debd50f23d389bd7fa93d060","filters_passed":["developer_intent","not_revert","not_merge","source_file_limit","function_limit","no_public_feature_addition","parse_before_after","not_generated","null_detector"],"intent_evidence":{"linked_issues":[],"message":"fix(express): stop reading a streamable file for a head request\n\nExpress answers HEAD requests with the GET route, so the stream of a\nStreamableFile was piped into the HEAD response. Node discards the body\nof a HEAD response without ever applying backpressure, so the pipe read\nthe whole source at full speed, whatever its size. Each HEAD request\ncost as much disk and CPU time as a full download, without the client\nhaving to receive anything.\n\nFor a HEAD request, the response now ends once the source is readable,\nand the source is then destroyed. Waiting for it keeps the error\nhandler's answer to a source that cannot be opened, such as the 400 for\na missing file. The status and headers sent are unchanged.\n\nDiscovered by Anthropic's OSS Scanner, as vulnerability ANT-2026-XZ3CL5Q9."},"language":"typescript","license":"MIT","pair_group":{"id":"refactor-4fa73f4c1292d638","kind":"refactor","repository":"nestjs/nest","samples":["8b8e8396f71d8903debd50f23d389bd7fa93d060:before","8b8e8396f71d8903debd50f23d389bd7fa93d060:after"]},"pair_group_id":"refactor-4fa73f4c1292d638","parent_sha":"97ab04494ca00c03d566d3225b7790c5415e36c9","pin_sha":"2eb7be8dc3410ac5b89aa84fd334e6813b53059c","repo":"nestjs/nest"}
